FR2-16 audit-5 (final escalation cycle) -- VERDICT: BLOCKED-REQUIRED

Core finding: fix-5's "allow-list, fail-closed" guard is not fail-closed. It only ever asks
"does this match an approved template?" for text that (a) contains one of 11 trigger words (or,
in 9 files, a flag-word + a closed reason-word list), AND (b) is not within 160 chars of any of
~45 NARRATIVE_RE anchors, 250 chars of "pinchtab", or 60 chars of a template. Anything outside
(a) is invisible; anything inside (b) is auto-approved. So it is still a vocabulary list -- the
deny-list moved from "bad phrasings" to "trigger words + narrative anchors", and both halves are
open-ended in exactly the way the redesign said a positive list would not be.

