Diagnosis for BLOCKED: the recurring failure across 5 audits is the premise that honesty of free
prose can be enforced by a regex-level classifier. A deny-list fails on synonyms; this allow-list
fails because deciding WHICH text needs approval is itself a vocabulary problem (trigger words +
narrative exemptions), with the same unbounded-synonym property. A genuinely closed design would
have to require every sentence in a fenced, marker-delimited boundary region to be a template
(and forbid topic prose elsewhere), or accept that this is a human-review property, not a CI check.
